@startuml Edit-Request-AlternateFlow
title Edit Pending Request - Alternate Flow

actor Employee as emp
participant "Intranet Portal" as portal
participant "VTS Application" as vts
participant "VTS Database" as db

emp -> portal: Click VTS link from intranet
portal -> vts: Redirect with employee credentials
vts -> vts: Verify authentication

vts -> db: Query employee vacation requests\n(last 6 months + future 18 months)
db -> vts: Return all vacation requests & statuses
vts -> emp: Display vacation request summary\nand current statuses

emp -> vts: Select a pending vacation request\nto edit
note right of emp: Request status: PENDING_APPROVAL

vts -> db: Retrieve full request details
db -> vts: Return request data\n(title, dates, comments, etc.)
vts -> emp: Display editable request view\n(title, dates, comments, deletion, withdrawal options)

emp -> emp: Review current request data
emp -> vts: Modify request information\n(title, comments, and/or dates)

note right of emp: Employee can also choose to:\n- Delete request\n- Withdraw request\n- Submit changes

emp -> vts: Submit modified request information

alt Employee chose to withdraw
  vts -> vts: Prompt for withdrawal confirmation
  emp -> vts: Confirm withdrawal action
  vts -> db: Update request status to WITHDRAWN
  db -> vts: Confirm status update
  vts -> emp: Return to VTS home page
  note right of vts: Request withdrawn successfully
  
else Employee submitted information changes
  vts -> vts: Validate updated request data\n(dates, hours, balance)
  
  alt Validation Failed
    vts -> vts: Identify validation errors
    vts -> emp: Redisplay editing page\nwith errors highlighted and explained
    note right of emp: Employee can correct information
  else Validation Successful
    vts -> db: Update VacationRequest\nwith modified information\n(title, comments, dates, etc.)
    db -> db: Store updated request
    db -> vts: Confirm update
    
    vts -> emp: Return to VTS home page\nwith confirmation message
    emp -> emp: Request updated successfully
  end
end

@enduml
